{"kind": "daily", "period": "2026-10-04", "prepared_on": "2026-10-04", "html": "<div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,'PingFang TC','Helvetica Neue',Arial,sans-serif;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;color:#16213e;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:800;color:#1a2b4a;border-left:5px solid #5b8def;padding-left:12px;margin:0 0 18px;\">📰 每日 AI 新聞 Top 10 · 2026-10-04</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#e8f4fb;border-left:5px solid #3f97c9;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#3f97c9;font-weight:800;\">1.</span> It's not AI anymore, it's 'super intelligence' (according to the White House)<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#2b7fb0;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">政策</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">白宮改口不說 AI，要稱「超級智慧」</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">The White House gathered nearly every major tech CEO, including Zuckerberg, Bezos, Musk and Anthropic's Dario Amodei, to sign an AI safety pledge that President Trump called \"morally binding.\" Trump also signed an executive order.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">白宮邀集幾乎所有大型科技公司執行長（包括祖克柏、貝佐斯、馬斯克與 Anthropic 的 Dario Amodei）簽署 AI 安全承諾，川普稱其「具道德約束力」，並同時簽署一項行政命令。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">TechCrunch</b> · <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/video/its-not-ai-anymore-its-super-intelligence-according-to-the-white-house/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#f2f6e8;border-left:5px solid #88a83f;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#88a83f;font-weight:800;\">2.</span> A model guide for the GPT-6 family<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#6e8c28;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">模型</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">GPT-6 系列模型指南</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">OpenAI explains how startups can choose GPT-6 models, tune reasoning effort, improve prompts and skills, coordinate tools, and prepare workflows for production.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">OpenAI 說明新創團隊如何挑選 GPT-6 模型、調整推理強度、改進提示與技能、協調工具，並為正式上線的工作流程做準備。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">OpenAI</b> · <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/practical-guide-building-gpt-6\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#f9edf6;border-left:5px solid #c56bb0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#c56bb0;font-weight:800;\">3.</span> OpenAI safety employee resigns, claiming the company's 'culture is broken'<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#b04b9b;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">產業</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">OpenAI 安全員工離職，稱公司「文化已壞」</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">David Robinson, who used to write the safety reports that accompanied OpenAI's major model releases, resigned this week and issued a dire warning in an editorial in The Atlantic.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">David Robinson 過去負責撰寫 OpenAI each 次重大模型發布隨附的安全報告，本週離職，並在《The Atlantic》發表評論文章提出嚴正警告。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">TechCrunch</b> · <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/03/openai-safety-employee-resigns-claiming-the-companys-culture-is-broken/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#eef4ff;border-left:5px solid #5b8def;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#5b8def;font-weight:800;\">4.</span> Apple will limit Mac disk access as AI agents 'substantially' increase risk<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#3b6cf6;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">資安</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">AI 代理大幅增加風險，Apple 將限縮 Mac 磁碟存取權限</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">Apple is adding new limits to \"full disk access\" on Mac so that only users who genuinely wish to grant an app that extraordinary level of access can do so, in response to risks posed by AI agents.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">因應 AI 代理帶來的風險，Apple 將為 Mac 的「完整磁碟取用權限」加上新限制，確保只有真正想授予 App 這種極高權限的使用者才能做到。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">The Verge</b> · <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/1004295/apple-limit-mac-disk-access-ai-agents\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#ecf7ef;border-left:5px solid #4caf72;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#4caf72;font-weight:800;\">5.</span> Muse Creates Detailed Profiles of All Your Friends and Family<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#1e9e57;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">產品</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">Muse 會為你的親友建立詳細檔案</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">Millions have downloaded Meta's AI agent Muse, but getting it to do your bidding comes with privacy costs.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">Meta 的 AI 代理 Muse 已有數百萬次下載，但要讓它替你辦事，需要付出隱私上的代價。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">Wired</b> · <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/muse-creates-detailed-profiles-of-all-your-friends-and-family/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#f1ecfb;border-left:5px solid #8a6bd8;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#8a6bd8;font-weight:800;\">6.</span> Amazon responds to data center backlash, says it no longer uses NDAs<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#6b3bf6;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">產業</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">Amazon 回應資料中心反彈，稱不再使用保密協議</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">AWS CEO Matt Garman tried to push back against widespread suspicion of data centers, saying Amazon no longer uses NDAs. He also warned in a long blog post that communities blocking projects risk harm to the US economy and national security.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">AWS 執行長 Matt Garman 試圖回應外界對資料中心的普遍疑慮，表示 Amazon 已不再使用保密協議，並在長篇部落格文章中警告，社區阻擋專案恐對美國經濟與國家安全造成傷害。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">TechCrunch</b> · <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/03/amazon-responds-to-data-center-backlash-says-it-no-longer-uses-ndas/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#e8f6f5;border-left:5px solid #2bb0a6;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#2bb0a6;font-weight:800;\">7.</span> A Flaw in ChatGPT's Mac App Could Have Let Hackers Grab Sensitive Data<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#0f9b9b;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">資安</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">ChatGPT Mac App 漏洞恐讓駭客竊取敏感資料</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">A recently patched vulnerability in a ChatGPT app shows that AI software is itself an inviting and vulnerable target, even as attention has focused on AI agents' hacking capabilities.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">一個近期已修補的 ChatGPT App 漏洞顯示，在大家聚焦於 AI 代理的駭客能力時，AI 軟體本身也是誘人且脆弱的攻擊目標。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">Wired</b> · <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/a-flaw-in-chatgpts-mac-app-could-have-let-hackers-grab-sensitive-data/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#fbf3e3;border-left:5px solid #d99b3f;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#d99b3f;font-weight:800;\">8.</span> Sean Parker is rebuilding Stability AI around music<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#b9791f;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">產業</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">Sean Parker 要以音樂為核心重建 Stability AI</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">Sean Parker, who once taught the music industry what asking for forgiveness looks like, is back with the labels' blessing and money.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">Sean Parker 曾讓音樂產業見識什麼叫「先做再道歉」，如今帶著唱片公司的認可與資金回歸，重整 Stability AI。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">TechCrunch</b> · <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/02/sean-parker-is-rebuilding-stability-ai-around-music/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#fdeef0;border-left:5px solid #e0738a;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#e0738a;font-weight:800;\">9.</span> Don't be fooled—LLMs don't reason<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#d83a5e;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">研究</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">別被騙了——大型語言模型並不會推理</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">An essay from someone who helped build the program behind the famous Move 37 in the 2016 Go match in Seoul argues that LLMs do not truly reason.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">一位曾參與打造 2016 年首爾圍棋對弈中「第 37 手」程式的作者撰文主張，大型語言模型並不是真的在推理。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">MIT Technology Review</b> · <a href=\"https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/10/02/1145639/dont-be-fooled-llms-dont-reason/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background:#edeefb;border-left:5px solid #6b72d6;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:11px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:800;color:#16213e;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"color:#6b72d6;font-weight:800;\">10.</span> The 7-year-old Nvidia Shield TV is now $100 more expensive due to AI<span style=\"display:inline-block;background:#fff;color:#5159c9;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:1px 8px;border-radius:20px;margin-left:5px;\">產品</span></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#5b6470;margin:3px 0 6px;\">推出 7 年的 Nvidia Shield TV 因 AI 漲價 100 美元</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#555c68;line-height:1.55;\">Launched in 2019, the Nvidia Shield TV Pro now retails for $299.99, as AI demand drives up the price of anything with memory.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:#8a909c;margin-top:3px;line-height:1.55;\">2019 年推出的 Nvidia Shield TV Pro 現售價 299.99 美元；AI 需求推升了所有含記憶體產品的價格。</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;\"><b style=\"color:#3b424f;\">Ars Technica</b> · <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/10/the-7-year-old-nvidia-shield-tv-is-now-100-more-expensive-thanks-to-ai/\" style=\"color:#3b6cf6;text-decoration:none;\">原文連結</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align:center;font-size:11.5px;color:#9aa1ad;padding-top:10px;\">由 AI News Digest 從各家 RSS 自動挑選、翻譯並寄送</div>\n</div>\n"}